(footprint "MOUSEBITE_6"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Six 0.6 mm NPTH perforations along the write-protect tab's break line. These were previously drawn as 0.6 mm circles on Edge.Cuts, i.e. as MILLED features - and JLCPCB's minimum internal routing feature is 1.0 mm (0.8 mm at surcharge), so a 0.6 mm milled circle is below what their router can cut. They would have drawn a DFM query, been silently omitted, or broken a bit. Omitted, the tab is a solid 7.4 mm slab of FR4 and the write-protect feature is dead on every board. As drilled holes 0.6 mm is routine. Placed at x = 45.2, y = 35.5 on the board.")
	(tags "mousebite perforation breakaway NPTH")
